    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "In the figure, $AC\\perp BD$ with $AB=10$, $BC=6$ and $CD=15$. The length of $AD$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-1997-r2/q05.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "17"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$\\sqrt{296}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$\\sqrt{312}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$\\sqrt{341}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "19"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Pythagoras twice",
        "body": "In right triangle $ABC$: $AC^2=10^2-6^2=64$, so $AC=8$. In right triangle $ACD$: $AD^2=8^2+15^2=64+225=289$, so $AD=17$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 17**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
