    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "A tailor wants to cut two semi-circles, as shown, with the same diameter from a cloth measuring 80 cm by 160 cm. The diameters, in cm, of the largest semi-circles are",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-1997-r2/q11.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "120"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "90"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "80"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "100"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "125"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Pythagoras with the centres",
        "body": "Let $R$ be the radius. In the figure the centre $C$ of the upper semicircle is on the top edge and the centre $O$ of the lower one is on the bottom edge, with $OC=2R$ (the semicircles touch). Horizontally the centres are $160-2R$ apart and vertically $80$ apart, so $(2R)^2=80^2+(160-2R)^2$. Expanding, $4R^2=6400+25600-640R+4R^2$, so $640R=32000$ and $R=50$. The diameter is $100$ cm.\n\n**Answer: (D) 100**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
    "difficulty": 3,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
  {
