    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The number of solutions to the equation $\\sqrt{x^4+16}=x^2-4$ is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "0"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "4"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Compare the two sides",
        "body": "For every real $x$, $\\sqrt{x^4+16}>\\sqrt{x^4}=x^2>x^2-4$, so the two sides are never equal. There are no solutions. (Squaring would give $x^4+16=x^4-8x^2+16$, i.e. $x=0$, but $x=0$ fails: $\\sqrt{16}=4\\neq-4$.)\n\n**Answer: (A) 0**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "algebra"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
  {
