    "grade": "10-12",
    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Two circles with centres at $A$ and $B$ touch at $T$. $BD$ is the tangent at $D$ (to the circle with centre $A$) and $TC$ is a common tangent. $AT$ has length 3 and $BT$ has length 2. The length of $CD$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-1997-r2/q13.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$\\frac43$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$\\frac32$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$\\frac53$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$\\frac74$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$\\frac85$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Similar triangles",
        "body": "Tangents are perpendicular to radii, so the angles at $T$ and $D$ are right angles. $AB=3+2=5$ and $AD=3$ (it is a radius, and $AD\\perp BD$), so $BD=\\sqrt{25-9}=4$. Triangles $BTC$ and $BDA$ are similar (common angle at $B$, right angles at $T$ and $D$), so $\\dfrac{TC}{DA}=\\dfrac{BT}{BD}=\\dfrac24$, giving $TC=\\frac32$. Tangent lengths from $C$ to the circle with centre $A$ are equal: $CD=CT=\\frac32$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $\\frac32$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
    "difficulty": 3,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
  {
    "id": "samf-senior-1997-r2-14",
