    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "$E$ is the midpoint of $AB$ and $D$ is the midpoint of $BC$. The right angles are as shown (the angle at $C$ is $90^\\circ$, and $AD\\perp CE$). If $AC$ has length 4, then the length of $AB$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-1997-r2/q14.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "30"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$2\\sqrt{13}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$3\\sqrt6$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$3\\sqrt5$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$4\\sqrt3$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Coordinates",
        "body": "Put $C=(0,0)$, $A=(0,4)$, $B=(b,0)$. Then $D=(\\frac b2,0)$ and $E=(\\frac b2,2)$. $AD\\perp CE$: $\\overrightarrow{AD}=(\\frac b2,-4)$ and $\\overrightarrow{CE}=(\\frac b2,2)$ have dot product $\\frac{b^2}4-8=0$, so $b^2=32$. Then $AB^2=b^2+16=48$ and $AB=4\\sqrt3$.\n\n**Answer: (E) $4\\sqrt3$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Similar triangles",
        "body": "$E$ is the circumcentre of the right triangle, so $EC=EA=EB$. Let $\\angle DAC=\\alpha$; then $\\angle DCE=\\alpha$ (as $AD\\perp CE$) and $\\angle ABC=\\angle ECB=\\alpha$. Triangles $ACD$ and $BCA$ are similar, so $\\frac{AC}{BC}=\\frac{CD}{AC}$, with $CD=\\frac12BC$: $BC^2=2AC^2=32$. Then $AB^2=32+16=48$.\n\n**Answer: (E) $4\\sqrt3$**"
      }
    ],
