    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Rearrange",
        "body": "$97y-97=1900-19x$, so $97(y-1)=19(100-x)$. Since 19 and 97 are coprime primes, $97\\mid100-x$ and $19\\mid y-1$. With $x\\ge1$, $100-x\\le99$, so $100-x\\in\\{0,97\\}$, i.e. $x=100$ or $x=3$. For $x=100$: $y=1$, sum $101$. For $x=3$: $97(y-1)=19\\cdot97$, $y=20$, sum $23$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 23**"
