      {
        "title": "Find the radius",
        "body": "The chord $XY=3$ subtends $120^\\circ$ at the point $P$ of the other circle's arc, so it subtends $360^\\circ-2\\cdot120^\\circ=120^\\circ$ at the centre $C$ of the circle containing the arc (the reflex angle at the centre is $240^\\circ$). Thus triangle $CXY$ has apex angle $120^\\circ$ and base 3: $R=\\dfrac{3/2}{\\sin60^\\circ}=\\sqrt3$."
      },
      {
        "title": "Lens area",
        "body": "The shaded lens consists of two equal circular segments, each cut off by chord $XY$ with central angle $120^\\circ$. One segment = sector $-$ triangle $=\\frac13\\pi R^2-\\frac12R^2\\sin120^\\circ=\\pi-\\frac12\\cdot3\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt3}2=\\pi-\\frac{3\\sqrt3}4$. The lens is twice this: $2\\left(\\pi-\\frac34\\sqrt3\\right)$.\n\n**Answer: (E) $2\\left(\\pi-\\frac34\\sqrt3\\right)$**"
